# Trusted runtime semantics
The semantic contract consists only of:
1. the precondition established by the fixed contract witness and invocation; and
2. the postconditions imposed by explicit runtime contract assertions and exception branches that feed them.

Do not infer an additional postcondition merely because other Python failures would terminate the evaluation
